<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baranya</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Baranya is a region between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/drava">Drava</a>, centred on the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pecs">Pécs</a>. Long part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-hungary">Kingdom of Hungary</a>, it was divided after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, with the north remaining in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> as Baranya county and a southern strip passing to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a> and now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a>. Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a> mines made it valuable in the post-war disputes.</p></div>
